{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-38532" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{x+y}4z\\,dz]dA\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $xy$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/state.json" "file_sha256" "8232365f0824ee8e3efca9bcbc93377493bd8a51d0866e142543776b75c05125"} {"question" "q-38532" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ and $y$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{x+y}4z\\,dz]dA & ={∬}_{D}[2{z}^{2}]_{z=0}^{z=x+y}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2((x+y)^{2}-0)\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2{x}^{2}+4xy+2{y}^{2}\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2{x}^{2}+4xy+2{y}^{2}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}2{x}^{2}+4xy+2{y}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}2{x}^{2}+4xy+2{y}^{2}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[2{x}^{2}y+2x{y}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=x}dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{x}^{2}(x-0)+2x({x}^{2}-0)+\\frac{2}{3}({x}^{3}-0)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{14}{3}{x}^{3}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[\\frac{7}{6}{x}^{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{6}({1}^{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/state.json" "file_sha256" "8232365f0824ee8e3efca9bcbc93377493bd8a51d0866e142543776b75c05125"} {"question" "q-38532" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "008f1a87f507aa25b1061efda298a6fd6c545a90fe630c1b87c9b7650538d05d"} {"question" "q-38532" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/state.json" "file_sha256" "8232365f0824ee8e3efca9bcbc93377493bd8a51d0866e142543776b75c05125"} {"question" "q-38532" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{15}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{32}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/state.json" "file_sha256" "8232365f0824ee8e3efca9bcbc93377493bd8a51d0866e142543776b75c05125"} {"question" "q-38532" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/state.json" "file_sha256" "8232365f0824ee8e3efca9bcbc93377493bd8a51d0866e142543776b75c05125"} {"question" "q-38783" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}30x\\,dV\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the type I region given by \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1-x,\\,0\\le z\\le 1-x-y}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/state.json" "file_sha256" "8232365f0824ee8e3efca9bcbc93377493bd8a51d0866e142543776b75c05125"} {"question" "q-38783" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}30x\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x-y}30x\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ and $y$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x-y}30x\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}[{\\int }_{0}^{1-x-y}30x\\,dz]dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}[30xz]_{z=0}^{z=1-x-y}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}30x(1-x-y)\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}30x-30{x}^{2}-30xy\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}30x-30{x}^{2}-30xy\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}30x-30{x}^{2}-30xy\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[30xy-30{x}^{2}y-15x{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=1-x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}30x(1-x)-30{x}^{2}(1-x)-15x(1-x)^{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}15{x}^{3}-30{x}^{2}+15x\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}15{x}^{3}-30{x}^{2}+15x\\,dx & ={[\\frac{15}{4}{x}^{4}-10{x}^{3}+\\frac{15}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{15}{4}-10+\\frac{15}{2})-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/state.json" "file_sha256" "8232365f0824ee8e3efca9bcbc93377493bd8a51d0866e142543776b75c05125"} {"question" "q-38783" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "008f1a87f507aa25b1061efda298a6fd6c545a90fe630c1b87c9b7650538d05d"} {"question" "q-38783" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/state.json" "file_sha256" "8232365f0824ee8e3efca9bcbc93377493bd8a51d0866e142543776b75c05125"} {"question" "q-38783" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "\\frac{15}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/state.json" "file_sha256" "8232365f0824ee8e3efca9bcbc93377493bd8a51d0866e142543776b75c05125"} {"question" "q-38783" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/state.json" "file_sha256" "8232365f0824ee8e3efca9bcbc93377493bd8a51d0866e142543776b75c05125"} {"question" "q-161488" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x+y}}2z\\,dz]dA\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $xy$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{2}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/state.json" "file_sha256" "8232365f0824ee8e3efca9bcbc93377493bd8a51d0866e142543776b75c05125"} {"question" "q-161488" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ and $y$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x+y}}2z\\,dz]dA & ={∬}_{D}[{z}^{2}]_{z=0}^{z=\\sqrt{x+y}}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}({(\\sqrt{x+y})}^{2}-0)\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x+y\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}x+y\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{2}}x+y\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{2}}x+y\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[xy+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y={x}^{2}}dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x({x}^{2}-0)+\\frac{1}{2}({x}^{4}-0)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}+\\frac{1}{10}{x}^{5}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(1-0)+\\frac{1}{10}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{20}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/state.json" "file_sha256" "8232365f0824ee8e3efca9bcbc93377493bd8a51d0866e142543776b75c05125"} {"question" "q-161488" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "008f1a87f507aa25b1061efda298a6fd6c545a90fe630c1b87c9b7650538d05d"} {"question" "q-161488" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/state.json" "file_sha256" "8232365f0824ee8e3efca9bcbc93377493bd8a51d0866e142543776b75c05125"} {"question" "q-161488" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{20}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{10}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/state.json" "file_sha256" "8232365f0824ee8e3efca9bcbc93377493bd8a51d0866e142543776b75c05125"} {"question" "q-161488" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{20}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/state.json" "file_sha256" "8232365f0824ee8e3efca9bcbc93377493bd8a51d0866e142543776b75c05125"} {"question" "q-161514" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/assets/330b550b31987e29aceb4b2a253e26ebec470692a6a0144f64725801f2df2b7d.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}x\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above. \n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the top one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/state.json" "file_sha256" "8232365f0824ee8e3efca9bcbc93377493bd8a51d0866e142543776b75c05125"} {"question" "q-161514" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/assets/03a91dfd9f6a69455157c47162b11cd69cb3b03cfabea2770b94f7322015b0e2.png)\n\n \nNotice that our solid can be written as the type I region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1+2y},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/assets/ac3eafe926b84588703bb8a56a1529ebe1352d25764a523b97c684a4f4e95201.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1+2y}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}x\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1+2y}x\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ and $y$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1+2y}x\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1+2y}x\\,dz]dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[xz]_{z=0}^{z=1+2y}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}x(1+2y)\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}x(1+2y)\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}x(1+2y)\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x[y+{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}6x\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}6x\\,dx & =[3{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/state.json" "file_sha256" "8232365f0824ee8e3efca9bcbc93377493bd8a51d0866e142543776b75c05125"} {"question" "q-161514" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "008f1a87f507aa25b1061efda298a6fd6c545a90fe630c1b87c9b7650538d05d"} {"question" "q-161514" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/state.json" "file_sha256" "8232365f0824ee8e3efca9bcbc93377493bd8a51d0866e142543776b75c05125"} {"question" "q-161514" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "20"] ["math" "24"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/state.json" "file_sha256" "8232365f0824ee8e3efca9bcbc93377493bd8a51d0866e142543776b75c05125"} {"question" "q-161514" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/state.json" "file_sha256" "8232365f0824ee8e3efca9bcbc93377493bd8a51d0866e142543776b75c05125"} {"question" "q-161517" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/assets/89fba52c9a48d4f8f2ddac0b060c3ffab7e3ba4f6652124f4a9ac6ba39a579e5.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}(3x-1)\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the top one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/state.json" "file_sha256" "8232365f0824ee8e3efca9bcbc93377493bd8a51d0866e142543776b75c05125"} {"question" "q-161517" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/assets/86c1bef04ebf536b10f3f7d61eafcff909bd439b7641cbfc31cecd05cca23c18.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type I region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2-x+y},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/assets/dfa0a80bc323401f050d1302dc42c92558d8b566d9b0f985e955d34eb5cc15bd.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2-x+y}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}(3x-1)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-x+y}(3x-1)\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $x$ and $y$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2-x+y}(3x-1)\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2-x+y}(3x-1)\\,dz]dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(3x-1)[z]_{z=0}^{z=2-x+y}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(3x-1)(2-x+y)\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3xy-y-3{x}^{2}+7x-2\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3xy-y-3{x}^{2}+7x-2\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}(3x-1)y+(-3{x}^{2}+7x-2)\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{3x-1}{2}\\,{y}^{2}+(-3{x}^{2}+7x-2)y]}_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2(3x-1)+2(-3{x}^{2}+7x-2)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}-6{x}^{2}+20x-6\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}-6{x}^{2}+20x-6\\,dx & =[-2{x}^{3}+10x-6x]_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(-2+10-6)-0 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/state.json" "file_sha256" "8232365f0824ee8e3efca9bcbc93377493bd8a51d0866e142543776b75c05125"} {"question" "q-161517" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "008f1a87f507aa25b1061efda298a6fd6c545a90fe630c1b87c9b7650538d05d"} {"question" "q-161517" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070095/state.json" "fil